1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,440
You’re sixteen, and the formulas keep coming.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,640
Pendulums.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,840
Gases.

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,340
Trigonometry.

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:20,029
What if you could discover them, instead of memorising them?

6
00:00:28,775 --> 00:00:33,215
In high school, the motto changes: discover the formula yourself.

7
00:00:33,275 --> 00:00:37,815
Change the launch angle and watch the range respond.

8
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:40,415
Two different angles hit the same target.

9
00:00:40,475 --> 00:00:42,615
Can you explain why?

10
00:00:42,675 --> 00:00:49,615
Change a pendulum’s length, and the clock’s rhythm changes with it.

11
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:58,673
Slope, derivative and area stop being symbols and become something you can see.

12
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:02,523
Some formulas come with centuries-old stories.

13
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:11,023
Measure a mountain and the horizon, and estimate the size of the Earth, like al-Biruni.

14
00:01:11,083 --> 00:01:19,023
Find your latitude and local time with an astrolabe.

15
00:01:19,083 --> 00:01:29,182
And explore sound waves, echoes and resonance with acoustic jars.

16
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:31,832
It’s not only about exams.

17
00:01:31,892 --> 00:01:38,532
Life-skills labs for young people let you practise communication, problem solving and decisions.

18
00:01:38,592 --> 00:01:40,932
Plan your week.

19
00:01:40,992 --> 00:01:43,332
Map your stress.

20
00:01:43,392 --> 00:01:45,932
Build a student budget.

21
00:01:45,992 --> 00:01:59,690
And the AI-literacy games show how a language model picks its next word, so you can use AI wisely.

22
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,940
Your progress is yours.

23
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,540
Your student profile stays private, and an optional photo never leaves your device.

24
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:12,940
Share cards leave out your school details unless you choose them.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,140
Your school number never appears on a card.

26
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:24,340
And the weekly top list? It’s off for new accounts until you turn it on.

27
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:30,198
Proud of your progress? Earn an achievement card anyone can verify by QR code.

28
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,048
Being a teenager at İDÜ Lab means this:

29
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,048
You don’t just learn the formula.

30
00:02:34,108 --> 00:02:38,048
You discover it.

31
00:02:38,108 --> 00:02:46,470
Got an idea for a game? Your teachers can build it in Guest Studio, no code needed.

